# ── Clinic web: one build, two sites ────────────────────────────────────
#
# A single deployment serves both the patient website and the staff portal.
# Point BOTH hostnames at the same static build; the app reads
# window.location.hostname and mounts the matching routes. There are no
# per-host rewrite rules to configure on any platform.
#
#   dr-asif-clinic.in            -> patient website        (/)
#   dashboard.dr-asif-clinic.in  -> staff portal           (/)
#
# DNS: both records point at the same host.
#   dr-asif-clinic.in            A/ALIAS -> your host
#   dashboard.dr-asif-clinic.in  CNAME   -> dr-asif-clinic.in
#
# The host must serve index.html for unknown paths (SPA fallback) on both
# hostnames -- the one thing it does need to know. Netlify: a _redirects
# line `/* /index.html 200`. Vercel: a rewrite to /index.html. nginx:
# `try_files $uri /index.html;`.

# Where the clinic API lives. One API serves both sites.
VITE_API_URL=https://api.dr-asif-clinic.in/api/clinic

# ── Site splitting (all optional) ───────────────────────────────────────

# Force one mode regardless of hostname. Leave unset for hostname
# detection. Useful to preview either site locally:
#   VITE_SITE_MODE=public  -> the patient site at localhost:5176/
#   VITE_SITE_MODE=portal  -> the portal at localhost:5176/
# Unset on localhost means 'both', which is how development has always
# worked: portal at /, patient site at /clinic.
# VITE_SITE_MODE=

# Exact hostnames, if the clinic's portal is not on a conventional
# subdomain. These win over the prefix convention.
# Recognised prefixes by default: dashboard, portal, admin, staff.
# VITE_PORTAL_HOSTS=staff.asifclinic.co.in,clinic-admin.example.in
# VITE_PUBLIC_HOSTS=asifclinic.co.in,www.asifclinic.co.in

# Absolute URLs for the cross-links between the two sites ("View public
# site" in the portal). Only needed when the two domains are unrelated --
# otherwise the portal subdomain is added/removed automatically.
# VITE_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://dr-asif-clinic.in
# VITE_PORTAL_SITE_URL=https://dashboard.dr-asif-clinic.in

# ── Platform subdomain addressing (multi-tenant) ──────────────────────
# Set these two and ONE build of this app serves every clinic:
#
#   acme.yourco.in         -> Acme's patient website
#   acme.portal.yourco.in  -> Acme's staff portal
#   bright.yourco.in       -> a different clinic, a different database
#
# The app reads its own hostname, asks the provider API's tenant
# directory which clinic that is, and points itself at that clinic's own
# API before rendering anything. VITE_API_URL above is then only the
# fallback for a clinic on its own domain.
#
# Leave BOTH unset for a single-clinic deployment -- the app skips the
# lookup entirely and uses VITE_API_URL, exactly as it did before.
# VITE_PLATFORM_DOMAIN=yourco.in
# VITE_PROVIDER_API_URL=https://console.yourco.in
